  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope — Four Categories of Employee Benefits" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Short-Term Employee Benefits" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Post-Employment Benefits — the State Basic Pension System" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Defined Benefit Plans — a Genuinely Narrow Category in China" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Termination Benefits" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Other Long-Term Employee Benefits" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Recognising Short-Term Compensation" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — State Basic Pension Contributions" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IAS 19" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">All forms of consideration for employee service</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 9 governs ALL forms of CONSIDERATION given by an ENTERPRISE in EXCHANGE for SERVICES rendered by EMPLOYEES, or for the TERMINATION of employment — BROADLY paralleling IAS 19's OWN four-category STRUCTURE internationally (short-term BENEFITS, post-employment BENEFITS, termination BENEFITS, other LONG-term benefits), though the PRACTICAL emphasis DIFFERS significantly GIVEN China's PREDOMINANTLY state-run PENSION system (Section 4).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Four Categories of Employee Benefits</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Mirroring IAS 19's structural categories</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Examples</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Short-term employee benefits</span><span>Wages, bonuses, statutory social insurance contributions, paid leave</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Post-employment benefits</span><span>Basic pension insurance contributions; supplementary enterprise annuity (see ASBE No. 10)</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Termination benefits</span><span>Payments made on termination of employment before the normal retirement date</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Other long-term employee benefits</span><span>Long-service awards and similar benefits not falling into the other three categories</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Short-Term Employee Benefits</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Recognised as an expense and liability as service is rendered</div><div class="text-supporting">SHORT-TERM employee BENEFITS — wages, BONUSES, and the ENTERPRISE'S own STATUTORY social INSURANCE contributions (MEDICAL, unemployment, WORK injury, MATERNITY insurance, PLUS the housing PROVIDENT fund) — are RECOGNISED as a LIABILITY and an EXPENSE in the PERIOD the EMPLOYEE renders the RELATED service, UNDISCOUNTED, given their SHORT-term settlement HORIZON.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Post-Employment Benefits — the State Basic Pension System</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Contributions to a state-managed pool, expensed as incurred</div><div class="text-supporting">The OVERWHELMING majority of Chinese ENTERPRISES participate in the STATE'S mandatory BASIC PENSION INSURANCE system — a STATE-managed, POOLED arrangement into WHICH the ENTERPRISE makes REGULAR contributions, WITHOUT retaining ANY further LEGAL or CONSTRUCTIVE obligation BEYOND those CONTRIBUTIONS. This is TREATED, in SUBSTANCE, as a DEFINED CONTRIBUTION plan — CONTRIBUTIONS are SIMPLY EXPENSED as INCURRED, WITH no ACTUARIAL valuation REQUIRED, CONSISTENT with IAS 19's OWN defined contribution TREATMENT internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Defined Benefit Plans — a Genuinely Narrow Category in China</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A structural feature of ASBE 9 that is rarely triggered in practice</div><div class="text-supporting">THIS Standard DOES contain a FRAMEWORK for DEFINED BENEFIT plans (REQUIRING actuarial VALUATION, discounting, and the SAME general MECHANICS found under IAS 19 internationally) — BUT, given the DOMINANCE of the STATE'S basic PENSION system DESCRIBED above, GENUINE corporate DEFINED BENEFIT pension OBLIGATIONS are a GENUINELY NARROW, comparatively RARE feature of Chinese enterprise ACCOUNTING, in CONTRAST to jurisdictions (SUCH as JAPAN or many WESTERN economies) WHERE legacy CORPORATE defined BENEFIT plans remain WIDESPREAD and MATERIAL.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Termination Benefits</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognised when the entity can no longer withdraw the offer</div><div class="text-supporting">TERMINATION benefits are RECOGNISED as a LIABILITY and EXPENSE at the EARLIER of: WHEN the ENTERPRISE can NO LONGER WITHDRAW its OFFER of THOSE benefits, or WHEN the ENTERPRISE recognises RELATED restructuring COSTS — CONSISTENT with IAS 19's OWN termination benefit RECOGNITION trigger internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Other Long-Term Employee Benefits</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A residual category for benefits not settled within twelve months</div><div class="text-supporting">OTHER long-TERM employee BENEFITS — such as LONG-SERVICE awards NOT expected to be WHOLLY settled WITHIN twelve MONTHS of the RELATED service being RENDERED — are MEASURED on a BASIS broadly SIMILAR to defined BENEFIT post-employment BENEFITS, though WITH a SIMPLIFIED recognition APPROACH for actuarial GAINS and LOSSES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Recognising Short-Term Compensation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A straightforward period expense</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Monthly wages and bonus accrual</div><div class="wk-body">A company's employees earn RMB 8,000,000 in wages for the month, plus an anticipated year-end bonus accrual of RMB 1,200,000 for the same month's service.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises a TOTAL short-term employee benefit EXPENSE and LIABILITY of RMB 8,000,000 + RMB 1,200,000 = <strong>RMB 9,200,000</strong> for the MONTH, RECOGNISED as the RELATED service is RENDERED, REGARDLESS of WHEN the AMOUNTS are ACTUALLY paid.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — State Basic Pension Contributions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A defined contribution expense, with no further obligation</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Monthly statutory pension insurance contributions</div><div class="wk-body">A company is required to contribute 16% of its total monthly payroll of RMB 10,000,000 to the state's basic pension insurance pool.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company EXPENSES RMB 10,000,000 × 16% = <strong>RMB 1,600,000</strong> for the MONTH as INCURRED — WITH NO FURTHER obligation or ACTUARIAL valuation REQUIRED, since the STATE pension SYSTEM is treated as a DEFINED CONTRIBUTION arrangement from the ENTERPRISE'S perspective.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 9 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Amounts of employee benefits payable, by category</span><span>Basic pension insurance and other social insurance contributions recognised as expense</span><span>Basis for any defined benefit obligation, where applicable</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether an arrangement is genuinely a defined contribution or defined benefit plan</span><span>Timing of termination benefit recognition</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Bonus accruals and expected short-term compensation amounts</span><span>Actuarial assumptions, where a genuine defined benefit obligation exists</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 19</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 9 vs IAS 19</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 9</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 19</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Four-category structure</span><span>Same categories</span><span>Same categories — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Practical dominance of defined benefit plans</span><span>Genuinely rare — state pension system dominates</span><span>Historically widespread in many jurisdictions</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">The ACCOUNTING framework is thoroughly CONVERGED — the MEANINGFUL practical DIFFERENCE lies in HOW frequently each CATEGORY actually ARISES, given China's STATE-dominated pension LANDSCAPE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every employee benefit event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Short-term/post-employment benefit expense</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Liability and expense recognised as service is rendered</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 10</span><span>Enterprise Annuity Fund — governs the supplementary, voluntary occupational pension vehicle some enterprises establish in addition to the state basic pension system</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 11</span><span>Share-based Payment — governs equity-based employee compensation, addressed separately from this Standard's general employee benefits scope</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Basic pension insurance (基本养老保险)</div><div class="glossary-def">China's mandatory, state-managed pension system, into which enterprises make contributions treated as a defined contribution arrangement.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Housing provident fund (住房公积金)</div><div class="glossary-def">A mandatory employer/employee-funded housing savings scheme in China, treated as a short-term employee benefit.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe09 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
